      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$\nthen\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$AB=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"5px\" align=\"left\">$\\,.$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 0 & -1\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1 \\\\ 0\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 0 & 0\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+0 & 0+2 \\\\ 0+0 & 0+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
